WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.467
-Today, Republicans exploded
into absolute chaos,

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:07.167
unlike here at this show,
on what was supposed to be

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.501
their first day in charge
of the House of Representatives

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.968
when a revolt by far-right
MAGA members

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:13.634
blocked GOP leader
Kevin McCarthy

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:14.667
from winning enough votes
to become

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.133
speaker
on the first two ballots.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:19.167
It's the first time the House
has failed to elect a leader

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.367
on the first ballot in a century
and will almost certainly lead

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.501
to even more
GOP infighting and chaos.

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:26.734
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:31.167
♪♪

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.400
It would take far too long

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.267
to recount all
the political tumult

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.000
we experienced
in the year 2022 --

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.534
the January 6th revelations,

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:40.868
the sedition charges
for insurrectionists,

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:42.634
the criminal charges
for Trump cronies,

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:44.300
the FBI's search of Mar-a-Lago,

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.300
the Supreme Court decision
overturning Roe v. Wade,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.367
the response
to Russia's war in Ukraine,

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.133
and the shocking
midterm election result

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:53.033
that defied decades
of historical precedent,

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.100
among many other things.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.400
Now, if, after all of that,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.767
you were hoping
that 2023 would usher

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.634
in a new era
of calm and normalcy,

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.400
then please allow me
to introduce you to one

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.968
Rudolph Giuliani, seen here,

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.934
realizing he wrote not just 2022
on a check today,

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:12.868
but also that he wrote "bribe"
in the memo.

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:16.901
Anyway, Rudy was at Mar-a-Lago

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.868
to celebrate New Year's
with a bunch of other normal,

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.567
well-adjusted people,
and to ring in the New Year,

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:24.067
he recorded and then posted
online a very bizarre video

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.801
where you can't hear
a word he's saying.

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:29.367
We're going to show you the
video he himself posted online.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.300
But again, none of this
will be intelligible to you

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.367
since he's completely drowned
out by the noise of the party,

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.100
but apparently
doesn't realize it.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.100
[ Loud, indistinct music
playing ]

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.834
-[ Indistinct ]

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:52.400
♪♪

00:01:52.400 --> 00:02:01.067
♪♪

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:03.100
-Hats off to the band
for playing "Footloose"

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.033
for a crowd
that is almost certainly

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.934
medically incapable
of doing the "Footloose" dance.

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:10.467
"Footloose" sounds
like an excuse

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:13.234
Rudy would give
for being late to a meeting.

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:14.701
"Sorry, boss.
I got a foot loose.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.400
The toes on the right one
are facing backwards,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.367
so even when I run,
I go in a circle."

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.801
Also, this is just
some advice for anyone

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.400
on any screen,
myself included.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.801
It's one of the first things
I learned in television.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.567
Never lead with your chin.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:31.501
No one's chin
is their finest attribute,

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.133
especially when
you're 78 years old.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.901
If you fell asleep during Fallon

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.467
and woke up to me
looking like that,

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:38.000
you would change
the channel immediately.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.467
Here, I'll prove it.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:40.667
Hey.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:44.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:46.601
What happened?

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.567
You fall asleep?

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:52.934
You fall asleep during Fallon?

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:59.567
Well, we're happy to have you.
Check out the show.

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.267
There is one more thing
I have to point out

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.601
before we move on -- Rudy,
has since deleted this video,

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:05.767
but when he originally
posted it on Twitter,

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:09.234
he did so with the caption --
and this is 100% real...

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:18.000
Either Rudy
forgot what year it was

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.767
or he successfully

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:22.868
traveled exactly one year
into the future.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.200
And honestly, I think
both explanations are feasible.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.367
If Rudy had a DeLorean,

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.734
I absolutely believe
he would use it

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:32.567
to travel a comically
insignificant amount of time.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:34.634
Rudy, where should we go?
Back to the Jurassic era?

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:38.033
Should we kill Hitler or should
we travel to the 30th century?

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:40.367
"I say we go one year
into the future.

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.434
I want to see
if my hair grows back.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:43.734
I've been covering it
in chia seeds

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.334
and watering it for weeks."

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:46.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.367
Now, Rudy may have been wrong
about what year it is,

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.834
but if today's stunning
political developments

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.234
are any indication,
I'm guessing his fellow

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.601
Republicans will give anything
to fast forward to 2024

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.367
because they're
currently embroiled

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:58.767
in a chaotic meltdown
over the future of their party.

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:00.467
On the very first day
they were supposed to be

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:01.934
in charge of the House
of Representatives,

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.868
GOP leader Kevin McCarthy
failed to win enough votes

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:07.267
on the first two ballots to
become Speaker of the House --

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:10.367
a monumental failure that
has not happened in 100 years.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:13.300
-Longtime Trump ally
Kevin McCarthy

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.133
is facing a revolt from
far-right members of his caucus

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:18.300
who think the party's
only mistake

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.767
is not doing more
to embrace Trumpism.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:23.534
-The results of this first round
of this high-stakes vote

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.734
for a new speaker
have now come in.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:28.801
Republican leader Kevin McCarthy
had hoped to take the gavel

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.400
immediately
after the first ballot.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.801
That will not happen.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.567
The voting
will continue this afternoon.

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:36.000
He faces an uphill battle
within his own party --

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.601
a select few against him,
but enough of them to keep him

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.167
from getting the votes
he needed.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:44.601
-Congressman Kevin McCarthy,
who can only afford

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:48.067
to lose four
House Republican votes

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:50.000
if he wants to become
the next speaker,

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.200
has lost five House Republican
votes,

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.934
six House Republican votes.

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:57.334
-McCarthy will not win
on the second ballot,

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:59.501
on the second vote
of the Republican Congress.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.234
-That's right.
GOP leader Kevin McCarthy,

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.868
who has been fanatically
pro-Trump and spent years

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.934
ingratiating himself to Trump
in the MAGA movement,

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:08.434
is facing a backlash from
far-right members

00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:11.100
of his own party who think
he's not pro-Trump enough.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.334
And if there's
one political lesson

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:13.868
we've learned
in the past six years

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:17.467
is that there is always
someone more pro-Trump whenever.

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:20.734
Whatever line of decency
you draw in your head,

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:23.367
someone else is gonna walk right
through that mother[bleep].

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:27.267
I mean, even Trump himself
knows there are people out there

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:28.501
more pro-Trump than him.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.667
I mean, people get
Donald Trump tattoos.

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.133
He wouldn't. He also couldn't.

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:34.767
His skinny so tough
you'd need a diamond-tip needle

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.400
just to leave a light smudge.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.868
So now McCarthy has already lost
at least the first two votes,

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:41.334
imperiling his bid
to become speaker

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:42.901
and throwing
the GOP conference into chaos.

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:45.400
In fact, House Republicans
on either side of the fight

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.100
have been bickering,
calling each other names

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.701
and accusing each other
of backstabbing and betrayal.

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:51.767
-There's nothing
that indicates to me

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.400
that he's going to
change his pattern

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.934
since he's been
in leadership

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:56.901
where he's part
of the swamp cartel.

00:05:56.901 --> 00:05:59.200
If you want to drain the swamp,

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.667
you cannot put
the biggest alligator

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:03.734
in charge of the exercise.
They're like.

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:07.267
Children. This is a this
is such a childish attempt

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:09.834
at gaining more
and more attention.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:11.367
You know why they say
it like that?

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.801
Because they want you
to interview them again.

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:15.100
That's why they're doing it.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:19.267
-I find out that it's my
Freedom Caucus colleagues

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:21.400
and my supposed friends
that went and did that.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.968
And they asked nothing for me.
Nothing.

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:26.534
That's what I found out
in there. I'm furious.

00:06:26.534 --> 00:06:28.834
-These people want to be taken
seriously as a governing party.

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:30.467
Meanwhile, they sound
like sorority members

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:32.434
who just got kicked out
for drinking too much.

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:34.400
"No one told me
there were any rules

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.734
against alcohol consumption.

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:38.934
And now I find out
from my supposed friends

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:40.701
that butt chugging is not
allowed?

00:06:40.701 --> 00:06:43.367
Well, I am furious."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.367 --> 00:06:45.834
Now, I'm not saying I'm enjoying
all this GOP infighting,

00:06:45.834 --> 00:06:47.534
but when I heard
about McCarthy's troubles,

00:06:47.534 --> 00:06:50.634
I did fly down to Mar-a-Lago
to party with Rudy Giuliani.

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:53.300
You should have seen us.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.834
We spent all night
pounding shots of whiskey

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:57.901
mixed with prune juice
and dancing

00:06:57.901 --> 00:06:59.334
to '80s movie soundtracks.

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:02.133
It was like if "White Lotus"
took place in a hospice.

00:07:02.133 --> 00:07:03.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:05.300
Ooh, who do you think
is going to die?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.868
Everyone eventually.

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:09.334
Now, as we're taping this, we
still don't know

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:11.767
the final outcome, because the
House will have to keep voting

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.834
until someone
is elected speaker.

00:07:13.834 --> 00:07:16.567
As of this afternoon, we don't
know when that will happen.

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:19.234
There's a chance you know
more about what happened

00:07:19.234 --> 00:07:20.934
as you're watching this
than we do taping it.

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:23.434
It's almost like you traveled
eight hours into the future

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:26.067
with Rudy Giuliani.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:28.501
In fact, the outcome
is so uncertain heading

00:07:28.501 --> 00:07:30.634
in today's vote that many,
including Fox News,

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:32.400
were predicting it
could take days

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.067
or even weeks
for the Republicans

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:35.400
to finally elect a speaker.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.801
-McCarthy needs the votes of all

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:39.334
but four House Republicans
to win the speakership,

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:43.200
but at least 5 and as many as
14 House Republicans oppose him.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.067
It could be the first time
in a century

00:07:45.067 --> 00:07:47.734
the speaker's vote isn't settled
on the first ballot.

00:07:47.734 --> 00:07:50.100
-Back in the Civil War times,

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:54.033
there was one speaker who was
not elected for two months

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:56.367
and it took 133 votes.

00:07:56.367 --> 00:07:57.534
-Alright, first of all,
it's not a great sign

00:07:57.534 --> 00:07:58.934
for your party's
political fortunes

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:01.067
when pundits are comparing
your situation

00:08:01.067 --> 00:08:03.701
to something that happened,
"back in the Civil War times."

00:08:03.701 --> 00:08:06.968
[ Laughter ]
Also, diggin' 2023 Steve Doocy

00:08:06.968 --> 00:08:08.467
talking like an old prospector

00:08:08.467 --> 00:08:10.534
huddled around a campfire
with a tin of beans.

00:08:10.534 --> 00:08:11.801
"Back in the Civil War times,

00:08:11.801 --> 00:08:14.300
there weren't no fancy phones
or gizmo.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.567
All we had was our wits.
Well, not all of us had them."

00:08:17.567 --> 00:08:19.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.934 --> 00:08:22.334
So much for my resolution --
to make less fun

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:24.501
of Rudy Giuliani this year.

00:08:24.501 --> 00:08:26.634
They all deserve this,
especially McCarthy,

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.067
who is so desperate for power

00:08:28.067 --> 00:08:30.367
he infamously flew down
to Mar-a-Lago

00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:32.801
for that embarrassing photo op
with Donald Trump

00:08:32.801 --> 00:08:35.534
just weeks after
the January 6th insurrection.

00:08:35.534 --> 00:08:36.968
Remember that?
McCarthy did everything

00:08:36.968 --> 00:08:38.234
he could to cozy up to Trump

00:08:38.234 --> 00:08:39.634
and the MAGA circus
in the House,

00:08:39.634 --> 00:08:41.534
and he's still facing a revolt

00:08:41.534 --> 00:08:43.234
from the looniest members
of the GOP.

00:08:43.234 --> 00:08:46.000
-He is, of course, gotten very
close to Donald Trump.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.934
He rehabilitated Donald Trump.

00:08:47.934 --> 00:08:50.567
I think all of these things
were in an effort

00:08:50.567 --> 00:08:53.434
to be able to, when the moment
came, to tell these people,

00:08:53.434 --> 00:08:55.501
"You can trust me,
I'm a conservative.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.968
I'm on your side.
I'm with the team."

00:08:57.968 --> 00:09:00.534
-I think all of those things
were explained by him

00:09:00.534 --> 00:09:05.267
wanting to be able to get the
gavel on the first ballot today.

00:09:05.267 --> 00:09:07.367
And if he doesn't,
and it's looking increasingly

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:09.434
like he won't,
this will be the first time

00:09:09.434 --> 00:09:11.300
we've seen this
in our lifetimes.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.968
This is only happened
once since the Civil War,

00:09:13.968 --> 00:09:16.167
and I think it will badly,
badly weaken him.

00:09:16.167 --> 00:09:18.200
-Did McCarthy think one visit
to Mar-a-Lago

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.934
was going to magically
solve everything?

00:09:19.934 --> 00:09:21.968
That place is the opposite
of Disney World.

00:09:21.968 --> 00:09:24.367
It's where dreams go to die.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:24.367 --> 00:09:26.501
Oh, so, no, wait. So it's
the same as Disney World.

00:09:26.501 --> 00:09:29.667
If you ever find yourself
at Mar-a-Lago

00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:31.868
and you're not wearing
a blue windbreaker

00:09:31.868 --> 00:09:33.334
with FBI on the back,

00:09:33.334 --> 00:09:36.868
that's how you know you took
some wrong turns in life.

00:09:36.868 --> 00:09:38.734
It's like waking up
at a hotel in Tijuana

00:09:38.734 --> 00:09:40.567
with a bag of white powder
on your nightstand,

00:09:40.567 --> 00:09:43.000
a stranger in your bathtub,
and loud knocking on the door

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.300
while someone yells,
"Policía. Abre la puerta."

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:47.667
You're not, when you hear that,
going to look in the mirror

00:09:47.667 --> 00:09:49.834
and think to yourself,
"This current year,

00:09:49.834 --> 00:09:53.400
2024, is off to a great start."

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.801
But maybe the craziest aspect
of this debacle

00:09:55.801 --> 00:09:57.834
was all the speculation
beforehand about who,

00:09:57.834 --> 00:10:00.167
if anyone, could beat McCarthy
if he lost the speaker vote.

00:10:00.167 --> 00:10:02.968
Several names
were floated before today.

00:10:02.968 --> 00:10:04.968
And on Fox News,
one of the far-right Republicans

00:10:04.968 --> 00:10:07.067
revolting against McCarthy
refused to rule out

00:10:07.067 --> 00:10:09.200
one of the most
farfetched hypotheticals

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.567
involving you know who.

00:10:10.567 --> 00:10:14.133
-I've heard from people at
the House Freedom Caucus

00:10:14.133 --> 00:10:16.534
that they like two names
out there --

00:10:16.534 --> 00:10:19.000
Steve Scalise and Donald Trump.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.767
-Well, I'm sure we do like it,
but I don't think

00:10:22.767 --> 00:10:24.067
they're the right people
for speaker.

00:10:24.067 --> 00:10:26.400
They may be, but we should
have a conversation.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.534
-That's right. Some of them
were actively floating Trump

00:10:28.534 --> 00:10:30.701
as a possible speaker of the
House before the votes today,

00:10:30.701 --> 00:10:32.634
because technically you don't
have to be a member of Congress.

